        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Limit new skill display names",
        "body": "Closes #77.\n\nAdds a shared 40-character skill display-name limit for hosted publishes and GitHub-backed sync. Existing over-limit hosted titles can be republished unchanged, but new or renamed hosted titles and synced GitHub titles are kept within the stored catalog limit.\n\nProof:\n- Backend publish on head `27f985a21857` rejects a new 41-character display name with `Display name must be 40 characters or less` before reading storage: `storage.get.calls=0`.\n- Hosted legacy behavior is preserved by the publish validator: unchanged 45-character legacy name reports `enforced=false`; a changed 45-character name reports `enforced=true`.\n- GitHub-backed sync with a 68-character frontmatter name plans a 40-character stored display name: `This Slug Is Also Longer Than Forty Char`, with `plan.stats={\"discovered\":1,\"inserted\":1,\"changed\":0,\"unchanged\":0,\"removed\":0}`.\n- Publish-form render proof passed for the inline 40-character validation and unchanged legacy over-limit path.\n- GitHub Actions on the pushed head have 23 passing non-Vercel checks; the remaining Vercel check is blocked on OpenClaw Foundation team authorization.",
